<title>FRANCE: Daewoo Securities may buy France's SMC - papers.</title>
<headline>Daewoo Securities may buy France's SMC - papers.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daewoo Securities Co, a unit of South Korea's Daewoo Group, is holding talks with the French government to buy bank Societe Marseillaise de Credit (SMC), French newspapers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Daewoo said recently that it was seeking to buy a bank in France or elsewhere in Europe.</p>
<p>Government officials were not available for comment.</p>
<p>SMC is in the process of being privatised. It lost 1.3 billion francs in 1994 and 952 million francs in 1995. In the first half of 1996, SMC posted a profit of 57 million francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
